[orch:err] ### milvus-io/milvus#51441 — enhance: force one row group per cell for the stats skip index (storage v2)
[orch:err] - State: `OPEN` · Closing-link from PR: no · Source: `cross`
[orch:err] - URL: https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/pull/51441
[orch:err] - Author: xiaofan-luan
[orch:err] - Labels: kind/enhancement, size/XXL, approved, area/internal-api, dco-passed, low-code-coverage
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] #### Issue body
[orch:err] ## What & why
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] `common.parquetStatsSkipIndex.enabled` builds chunk-level skip metrics from parquet footer statistics for storage-v2 sealed segments. The old implementation was unsafe: row-group statistics could be associated with the wrong cache cell and several metric implementations could return false negatives, so enabling the flag could silently drop matching rows. Even when pruning was correct, several execution paths still materialized the skipped cells and paid the object-storage IO.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] This PR makes the storage-v2 stats skip index safe, makes pruning avoid IO on the paths queries actually execute, and adds collection-level observability for both pruning effectiveness and scanned bytes.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] issue: #51440
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] ## Correctness
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] - Force one row group per cache cell only for column groups containing a type supported by the stats skip index. Footer statistics and cache cells are therefore aligned 1:1; vector-only and otherwise unsupported groups keep their normal packing.
[orch:err] - Keep parquet footer metadata alive while building VARCHAR metrics, then deep-copy the bounds. This removes the BYTE_ARRAY `string_view` lifetime bug.
[orch:err] - Fix BOOL `IN`, empty-string VARCHAR `IN`, missing min/max, physical-type mismatch, and stale metrics after column replacement. Unsupported or invalid statistics conservatively degrade to no pruning.
[orch:err] - Disable skip-index pruning for **all arithmetic predicates**. Arithmetic expressions still execute normally, but they do not install a skip callback and therefore cannot cause overflow/truncation-based false negatives or pollute skip-index effectiveness metrics.
[orch:err] - Preserve SQL three-valued logic: nullable predicates that observe validity (for example through `NOT`) still load validity data when a data cell is skipped.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] ## IO saving
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] Pruning decisions now happen before a sealed cell is pinned/materialized on both sequential scans and offset-input/iterative-filter scans. The scan, driver-prefetch, and default fallback-prefetch paths use the same skip decision, so a pruned cell is not fetched by a later stage.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] VARCHAR `IN` uses an owned `std::string` skip list on both scan and prefetch paths. This fixes the previous `std::string`/`std::string_view` mismatch that made the executed scan fetch cells the prefetch path had skipped.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] ## Storage-cost validity and aggregation
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] Scanned-byte values now carry an explicit `storage_cost_valid` bit from segcore through QueryNode reduction, streaming, delegator reduction, Proxy metrics, response `ExtraInfo`, and the HTTP handler.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] - Validity is AND-reduced across every worker/segment contribution; a missing field from an older node is `false`, which is safe during rolling upgrades.
[orch:err] - Growing/in-memory segments are valid zero-cost inputs. A sealed segment is valid only when its cache slots were created with storage usage tracking enabled.
[orch:err] - Partial accepted search results invalidate the aggregate instead of publishing a partial total as complete.
[orch:err] - Zero-hit query results retain their segment cost contribution.
[orch:err] - Two-phase retrieve includes `RetrieveByOffsets` IO.
[orch:err] - QueryStream preserves zero-hit contributions, validity across cache merges and split frames, and treats old workers that emit no frame as invalid.
[orch:err] - Empty delete frames contribute their storage cost without creating delete work.
[orch:err] - Proxy and HTTP no longer re-read the live config as a second reporting gate; they trust the validity attached to the result actually measured by QueryNode.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] `queryNode.segcore.tieredStorage.storageUsageTrackingEnabled` now defaults to **true** and is **startup-only**. Every cache slot therefore uses one process-start snapshot; runtime config changes cannot create partially measured results inside a node.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] ## Metrics and labels
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] - `internal_core_skipindex_chunks{skipindex_chunks="scanned"|"pruned",db_name,collection_name}` counts chunks actually judged by an available skip index.
[orch:err] - `internal_core_skipindex_prune_ratio{skipindex="prune_ratio",db_name,collection_name}` records the per-expression prune…
